# Two instances meet by Direct Connect, and a closing on character select
# returns b to DIRECT CONNECT's hub with the connection lost, for
# tools/a11y/drive_net.py --direct: each boots into the hub with a fresh code,
# a waits for a call and b dials a's code. They meet only through the
# router's public address, so the router must loop its own address back in
# (NAT loopback); the maintainer's does that for ports it forwards, so UDP
# 42050 and 42051 are forwarded to this machine.
#   python tools/a11y/drive_net.py --direct --muted tools/a11y/direct_lost.drive
# tools/a11y/direct_back.drive checks the other return. Instance b may be a
# base port build (--base-b): only the fork speaks, so b's speech waits are
# b-fork steps and its b-base steps wait on the scene instead. No step
# presses Y or chooses the clipboard row: both use the real clipboard. Up
# from the hub's top row wraps to its last, "Wait for a friend to call me",
# whatever rows the clipboard and recent opponents add above.

a wait "lobby: direct connect hub" 60
b wait "lobby: direct connect hub" 60
sleep 1

# a waits: the call's opening, its status line with its clock and buttons.
a press DUp
a press A
a wait "lobby: direct connect waiting as '"
a wait '\[a11y\] speak interrupt.*: "(Joining the online network\.\.\.|Waiting for a friend to call you) 0:00\. Y: copy my code B: stop"$' 5

# b goes to "Enter a friend's code", the row above the last, and types a's
# code on the code keyboard.
b press DUp
b press DUp
b press A
sleep 0.5
b dial a
b-fork wait '\[a11y\] speak interrupt.*: "(Joining the online network\.\.\.|Calling #[A-Z2-7]{3}-[A-Z2-7]{3}-[A-Z2-7]{2}) 0:00\. Y: copy my code B: stop"$' 5

# Each finds the other on the DHT and says hello to its public address; the
# router has to send those packets back in. Then the session: connecting
# shows the base port's line for a call with no reason, starting its
# countdown, and both enter character select.
a wait "match: recv valid MatchHello" 180
b wait "match: recv valid MatchHello" 60
a wait "net: rollback with" 60
b wait "net: rollback with" 60
a wait '\[a11y\] speak queue.*: "Searching for an opponent\.\.\."$' 5
b-fork wait '\[a11y\] speak queue.*: "Searching for an opponent\.\.\."$' 5
a wait '\[a11y\] speak queue.*: "Starting in 1\.\.\."$' 5
b-fork wait '\[a11y\] speak queue.*: "Starting in 1\.\.\."$' 5
a wait "lobby: entering CSS" 60
b wait "lobby: entering CSS" 60
# Either copy can be player 1: the one with the smaller key hosts
# (net_match.c), and each run's keys are fresh.
a wait '"Character select\. Player [12], no character\.'
b-fork wait '"Character select\. Player [12], no character\.'
b-base wait 'boot scene: state \d+ scene 8$'
sleep 2

# a closes on character select, and b returns to the hub, its top row now a
# as a recent opponent.
a quit
b wait "net: peer left" 30
b wait "lobby: direct connect hub, 1 recent, clipboard -$" 30
b-fork wait '\[a11y\] speak interrupt.*: "Connection lost\. DIRECT CONNECT\. PLAYER#[A-Z2-7-]+ played 0m ago"$' 5
sleep 1
